{"duration_api_ms":75691,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"04ad781d-657f-440f-a1c5-499d632f0198","total_cost_usd":1.6296700000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67375,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5643,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2456},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67375,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5643,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67375},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5643,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67375,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.6296700000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2456,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"schema\":\"agent-ee.review/1\",\"candidate_id\":\"62f16f3261185780b238caa726245d57ddcd2230c124e5e360b89aef094fd927\",\"run_id\":\"f532d848-7cf2-459a-bb11-b54997995f96\",\"packet_sha256\":\"92741503847da7f4c9b66286d57beadc968cc551e2a64f390319128014dd0733\",\"role\":\"circuit\",\"coverage\":[\"Compared declared fixture requirements (inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md) against the saved schematic and board component values.\",\"Read the full native schematic (inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch): symbol values, label connectivity (IN/OUT/GND), power flags, and pin assignments of R1, C1, J1.\",\"Read the full native board (inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb): pad-to-net assignments, track segments and widths, via, edge cuts, and the saved B.Cu GND zone filled polygon; manually traced GND return path C1.2 -> track -> via (113,100) -> B.Cu zone -> J1.3 thermal spokes.\",\"Cross-checked the exported XML netlist (work/netlist/design.xml) and connectivity.json against both the schematic and the board pad nets; topology is consistent (R1: /IN-/OUT, C1: /OUT-GND, J1 pins 1/2/3 = /IN,/OUT,GND).\",\"Reviewed the ngspice deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir), control script, log and measurements; independently recomputed the analytic step response for R=100k, C=100n (1-exp(-0.1)=0.09516 at 1 ms; 1-exp(-0.5)=0.39347 at 5 ms) and confirmed both match the recorded measurements, validating the simulation model, stimulus and .meas method.\",\"Checked geometry results (work/geometry/geometry.json) against the board file: all 5 segments 0.25 mm >= 0.2 mm requirement; segment/via/zone counts consistent with the native board.\",\"Reviewed ERC and DRC reports and their ignored-check lists for anything that could mask a real violation; none of the ignored categories are implicated by this design.\"],\"limitations\":[\"work/rc-step/result.raw is binary and was not read; measurement values were verified against work/rc-step/ngspice.log and independent analytic calculation instead.\",\"Stock symbol/footprint library files referenced by the sandbox environment are not included in the packet; footprint definitions were reviewed as embedded in the board file.\",\"Zone fill connectivity was assessed from the saved filled_polygon geometry by inspection; no refill or computational connectivity pass was possible (read-only candidate, no tools).\",\"Per the declared scope, only the ideal unloaded step response is covered; tolerance, temperature, loading, ADC sampling, EMI and hardware behavior remain unverified.\",\"Tool execution integrity (hashes, sandbox records) was taken as recorded; I could not re-run any tool to reproduce outputs.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"CKT-001\",\"title\":\"R1 populated as 100 kOhm instead of intended 10 kOhm; step response fails the declared 1 ms limit by ~6.6x\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch (symbol R1, uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78, property Value \\\"100k\\\")\",\"condition\":\"The declared requirement (fixture-requirements.md item 1) requires 0.62 V <= V(/OUT) <= 0.65 V at t = 1 ms after an ideal 1 V step, with an intended design of R1 = 10 kOhm, C1 = 100 nF (tau = 1 ms). The saved schematic and board both carry R1 = 100k, giving tau = R*C = 100e3 * 100e-9 = 10 ms.\",\"mechanism\":\"With tau = 10 ms, the unloaded output at 1 ms is V = 1 - exp(-1e-3/10e-3) = 1 - exp(-0.1) = 0.09516 V. The captured ngspice transient measured vout_1ms = 0.0951625 V, matching my analytic value to 5 significant figures, and vout_5ms = 0.3934693 V matches 1 - exp(-0.5) = 0.39347, independently confirming tau = 10 ms. The response is therefore far below the required 0.62-0.65 V window; the correct 10 kOhm value would yield 1 - exp(-1) = 0.6321 V, inside the window.\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 1: 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V; intended R1 = 10 kohm, C1 = 100 nF\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol Device:R uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78, property Value \\\"100k\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"footprint Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5, property Value \\\"100k\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\"line \\\"R1 IN OUT 100k\\\" and \\\"C1 OUT 0 100n\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"vout_1ms = 9.516251e-02, vout_5ms = 3.934693e-01\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/design.xml\",\"locator\":\"comp ref R1 value 100k; nets /IN (R1.1), /OUT (R1.2, C1.1)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The simulation deck faithfully reflects the native netlist topology and populated values, the 1 ns-rise PWL stimulus and 5 us timestep are appropriate for a 10 ms time constant, and both .meas results match closed-form RC theory exactly, so the verification itself is sound. The violation traces unambiguously to the component value in the native source files: R1 is 10x the intended value. Blocking because the fixture's single quantitative electrical requirement is missed by roughly a factor of 6.6 (0.095 V vs 0.62 V minimum), and the fix (change R1 to 10k) changes the schematic, board value field, and BOM.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"62f16f3261185780b238caa726245d57ddcd2230c124e5e360b89aef094fd927","run_id":"f532d848-7cf2-459a-bb11-b54997995f96","packet_sha256":"92741503847da7f4c9b66286d57beadc968cc551e2a64f390319128014dd0733","role":"circuit","coverage":["Compared declared fixture requirements (inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md) against the saved schematic and board component values.","Read the full native schematic (inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch): symbol values, label connectivity (IN/OUT/GND), power flags, and pin assignments of R1, C1, J1.","Read the full native board (inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb): pad-to-net assignments, track segments and widths, via, edge cuts, and the saved B.Cu GND zone filled polygon; manually traced GND return path C1.2 -> track -> via (113,100) -> B.Cu zone -> J1.3 thermal spokes.","Cross-checked the exported XML netlist (work/netlist/design.xml) and connectivity.json against both the schematic and the board pad nets; topology is consistent (R1: /IN-/OUT, C1: /OUT-GND, J1 pins 1/2/3 = /IN,/OUT,GND).","Reviewed the ngspice deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir), control script, log and measurements; independently recomputed the analytic step response for R=100k, C=100n (1-exp(-0.1)=0.09516 at 1 ms; 1-exp(-0.5)=0.39347 at 5 ms) and confirmed both match the recorded measurements, validating the simulation model, stimulus and .meas method.","Checked geometry results (work/geometry/geometry.json) against the board file: all 5 segments 0.25 mm >= 0.2 mm requirement; segment/via/zone counts consistent with the native board.","Reviewed ERC and DRC reports and their ignored-check lists for anything that could mask a real violation; none of the ignored categories are implicated by this design."],"limitations":["work/rc-step/result.raw is binary and was not read; measurement values were verified against work/rc-step/ngspice.log and independent analytic calculation instead.","Stock symbol/footprint library files referenced by the sandbox environment are not included in the packet; footprint definitions were reviewed as embedded in the board file.","Zone fill connectivity was assessed from the saved filled_polygon geometry by inspection; no refill or computational connectivity pass was possible (read-only candidate, no tools).","Per the declared scope, only the ideal unloaded step response is covered; tolerance, temperature, loading, ADC sampling, EMI and hardware behavior remain unverified.","Tool execution integrity (hashes, sandbox records) was taken as recorded; I could not re-run any tool to reproduce outputs."],"findings":[{"id":"CKT-001","title":"R1 populated as 100 kOhm instead of intended 10 kOhm; step response fails the declared 1 ms limit by ~6.6x","location":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch (symbol R1, uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78, property Value \"100k\")","condition":"The declared requirement (fixture-requirements.md item 1) requires 0.62 V <= V(/OUT) <= 0.65 V at t = 1 ms after an ideal 1 V step, with an intended design of R1 = 10 kOhm, C1 = 100 nF (tau = 1 ms). The saved schematic and board both carry R1 = 100k, giving tau = R*C = 100e3 * 100e-9 = 10 ms.","mechanism":"With tau = 10 ms, the unloaded output at 1 ms is V = 1 - exp(-1e-3/10e-3) = 1 - exp(-0.1) = 0.09516 V. The captured ngspice transient measured vout_1ms = 0.0951625 V, matching my analytic value to 5 significant figures, and vout_5ms = 0.3934693 V matches 1 - exp(-0.5) = 0.39347, independently confirming tau = 10 ms. The response is therefore far below the required 0.62-0.65 V window; the correct 10 kOhm value would yield 1 - exp(-1) = 0.6321 V, inside the window.","severity":"blocking","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md","locator":"requirement 1: 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V; intended R1 = 10 kohm, C1 = 100 nF"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol Device:R uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78, property Value \"100k\""},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb","locator":"footprint Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric uuid 8404a180-a151-464e-8f25-8cf316cdcba5, property Value \"100k\""},{"path":"work/rc-step/deck.cir","locator":"line \"R1 IN OUT 100k\" and \"C1 OUT 0 100n\""},{"path":"work/rc-step/ngspice.log","locator":"vout_1ms = 9.516251e-02, vout_5ms = 3.934693e-01"},{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"comp ref R1 value 100k; nets /IN (R1.1), /OUT (R1.2, C1.1)"}],"reasoning":"The simulation deck faithfully reflects the native netlist topology and populated values, the 1 ns-rise PWL stimulus and 5 us timestep are appropriate for a 10 ms time constant, and both .meas results match closed-form RC theory exactly, so the verification itself is sound. The violation traces unambiguously to the component value in the native source files: R1 is 10x the intended value. Blocking because the fixture's single quantitative electrical requirement is missed by roughly a factor of 6.6 (0.095 V vs 0.62 V minimum), and the fix (change R1 to 10k) changes the schematic, board value field, and BOM."}]}